# But What is AI?

#### Knowing the definition of a thing doesn't mean you *really* know what it is. Let's take some time to dive into what AI is and get an introduction to how it works.

#### In order to do that, you'll be working through Code,org's **AI for Oceans** activity over the upcoming levels.

#### **AI for Oceans** is a self-paced curriculum offering designed for students grades 3 through 12. In this fun introduction to artificial intelligence, you train a real machine learning model to identify sea creatures and trash in the ocean. Along the way you'll learn how AI works.

<p style="text-align:center;">
<img src="https://images.code.org/db2d5774622a56b85a5df8dc48d6d337-Screenshot 2026-02-18 at 11.16.38 AM.png"></p>

#### Even if you've seen this activity before, or had your students do it themselves, we recommend that you take the time to work through the activity again and take this opportunity to focus on increasing your own knowledge of how AI works.

#### If need to, you can skip ahead to the next section of this professional learning - Large Language Models.

